    <statement><p>Find a possible equation for the linear function <m>g(x,y)</m> shown in the
graph below:</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap12Sec4__Q21__pg-image-1.png" width="41%"/>
<p><m>g(x,y) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1x+1y+-2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>-1</m> in the <m>x</m> direction and a slope of
<m>1</m> in the <m>y</m> direction,
so <m>g(x,y) =  -   x  +   y + c</m>.
Since <m>g(0,0) = -2</m>, the formula is <m>g(x,y) =  -   x  +   y -2</m>.




</solution>
